# The vendored proposal agent is a byte-for-byte copy of Proposals/, and
# lib/proposalDoc/__tests__/vendored.test.ts hashes it to prove that. Line-ending
# normalisation would rewrite those bytes on checkout and break the comparison —
# and leave the browser running Python no pytest suite has seen in that form.
# Treat the whole vendored tree as opaque.
public/proposal/** -text

# ...and the same for the source it mirrors. With core.autocrlf on, git would
# hand out CRLF copies of these on checkout while the mirror stayed LF, so the
# two would no longer be byte-identical and the comparison would fail on any
# fresh clone. It also protects the binaries in here that git does not
# recognise as such -- the reference PDF among them.
Proposals/** -text

# The shipped workbooks and the Word template are binary; say so explicitly so
# no future core.autocrlf setting can corrupt them.
*.xlsx binary
*.xlsm binary
*.docx binary
*.pdf binary
